### double quotes inside a single-quoted option
flags='--title="Monthly Summary"'
pandoc $flags report.md
>>> SC2086 2:8
>>> SC2089 1:7
>>> SC2090 2:8

### single quotes after an equals sign
flags="--filter='status=open'"
tracker $flags
>>> SC2089 1:8
>>> SC2090 2:9

### taint propagates into another variable
target='old\ logs'
cleanup="rm -rf $target"
$cleanup
>>> SC2089 1:8
>>> SC2090 3:1

### escaped space in a single-quoted value
target='old\ logs'
rm $target
>>> SC2086 2:4
>>> SC2089 1:8
>>> SC2090 2:4

### single-quoted segment between slashes
backup="/mnt/'usb drive'/backups"
rm -r $backup
>>> SC2086 2:7
>>> SC2089 1:9
>>> SC2090 2:7

### tainted value passed double-quoted is fine
flags='--title="Monthly Summary"'
pandoc "$flags" report.md
>>> none

### array with quote in element passed quoted
flags=('--define=')
pandoc "${flags[@]}" report.md
>>> none

### apostrophe between letters is fine
message="it's done now"
notify $message
>>> SC2086 2:8

### tainted value given to eval is fine
flags='--title="Monthly Summary"'
eval pandoc $flags report.md
>>> SC2086 2:13

### length expansion does not propagate taint
target='old\ logs'
cleanup="rm -rf ${#target}"
$cleanup
>>> none

### length expansion of tainted path
backup="/mnt/'usb drive'/backups"
rm -r ${#backup}
>>> none

### sh dialect suggests positional parameters
#!/bin/sh
flags='--title="Monthly Summary"'
pandoc $flags report.md
>>> SC2086 3:8
>>> SC2089 2:7
>>> SC2090 3:8
